  {
   "id": "m2",
   "item": "17",
   "item_number": "4.1",
   "item_title": "Ontario Reformatory Heritage Conservation District - Draft Plan and Guidelines, 2024-487",
   "name": "Additional Motion",
   "moved_by": "Caton",
   "seconded_by": "Goller",
   "text": "City Council recognizes the requests of The Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation to the City of Guelph and the support of the Six Nations of the Grand River, as well as the ecological, social, reconciliation and economic benefits of a national urban park in Guelph and move to support Urban Park Guelph and the premise of House of Commons petition E-4593, notwithstanding other public uses or current staff direction.",
   "text_html": "<ol>\n<li>City Council recognizes the requests of The Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation to the City of Guelph and the support of the Six Nations of the Grand River, as well as the ecological, social, reconciliation and economic benefits of a national urban park in Guelph and move to support Urban Park Guelph and the premise of House of Commons petition E-4593, notwithstanding other public uses or current staff direction. </li>\n</ol>",
   "post_html": "<p>Councillor Allt raised a point of order, suggesting that the discussion was out of order because it was unrelated to the motion on the floor.  Mayor Guthrie ruled in favour of the point of order and asked City Council to focus the discussion on the motion on the floor.  </p>",
   "result": {
    "text": "",
    "label": "Out of order",
    "for": null,
    "against": null,
    "outcome": "Out of order",
    "inferred": false
   },
   "votes": {
    "for": [],
    "against": [],
    "other": []
   },
   "inherited": false,
   "recording": "unrecorded"
  },
  {
   "id": "m3",
   "item": "17",
   "item_number": "4.1",
   "item_title": "Ontario Reformatory Heritage Conservation District - Draft Plan and Guidelines, 2024-487",
   "name": "Amendment",
   "moved_by": "Gibson",
   "seconded_by": "O'Rourke",
   "text": "City Council recognizes the requests of The Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation to the City of Guelph and the support of the Six Nations of the Grand River, as well as the ecological, social, reconciliation and economic benefits of a national urban park in Guelph and move to support in principle Urban Park Guelph and the premise of House of Commons petition E-4593, notwithstanding other public uses or current staff direction.",
   "text_html": "<ol>\n<li>City Council recognizes the requests of The Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation to the City of Guelph and the support of the Six Nations of the Grand River, as well as the ecological, social, reconciliation and economic benefits of a national urban park in Guelph and move to support <strong>in principle </strong>Urban Park Guelph and the premise of House of Commons petition E-4593, notwithstanding other public uses or current staff direction. </li>\n</ol>",
   "post_html": "",
   "result": {
    "text": "Carried (12 to 0)",
    "label": "12-0",
    "for": 12,
    "against": 0,
    "outcome": "Carried",
    "inferred": false
